id: pm-1du7s3
title: Unknown-option refusals on extension commands with declared flags carry code unknown_option and list only the flags the command accepts
description: "Shippable tranche of pm-4of199 (2026-11-07). On an extension-created command that declares flags, an undeclared option was refused with an untyped command_failed and a list of every host definition it is validated against, including --no-extensions and, on a non-read command, the read-output controls the command refuses. The refusal now carries code unknown_option with the refused flag, and lists the command's declared flags followed by the host flags it inherits, from the same declaration pm contracts publishes as inherited_flags. The dynamic-dispatch refusal for a command without declared flags gets the same code and host-flag list. Refusing undeclared options on a zero-flag command's handler path is NOT part of this tranche: a census of the package fleet found released packages that read options they never declare, so that flip stays on pm-4of199 behind the fleet migration item."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,extensions,flags,validation
created_at: "2026-11-07T17:17:57.100Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-07T19:07:17.432Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-07T19:07:16.610Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-07T19:07:16.610Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: "pm <ext-cmd> --bogus on a command with declared flags exits 2 with code unknown_option and flag --bogus; The refusal lists the declared flags, then the inherited host flags, never --no-extensions, and read-output controls only on a command that declares read_output; The dynamic-dispatch zero-flag refusal carries the same code and host-flag list; A built-CLI integration spec covers a non-read and a read_output command"
parent: pm-4of199
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "validateLooseCommandOptionsWithFlagDefinitions takes a LooseOptionRefusalListing and refuses with code unknown_option and the flag. resolveCommandRefusalListing (src/cli/main.ts) supplies declared flags plus inherited host flags (no --no-extensions; read-output controls only with read_output) at the preAction, wrapper and dynamic extraction sites. The dynamic zero-flag refusal carries the same code and list. The handler-path zero-flag refusal stays on the parent until the fleet migration child lands."
expected_result: pm <ext-cmd> --bogus on a command with declared flags exits 2 unknown_option listing only its declared and inherited host flags
actual_result: "Built-CLI spec shows declared flags first, then host flags, without --no-extensions or read-output controls on a non-read command, and with them on a read_output command"
