comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T17:52:55.389Z","harness:claude-code","Implemented on branch fix/cli-option-contract-truthfulness. validateLooseCommandOptionsWithFlagDefinitions takes an optional LooseOptionRefusalListing, and its unknown-option refusal now carries code unknown_option, the flag, and a required line pointing at pm contracts --command. resolveCommandRefusalListing (src/cli/main.ts) supplies it at all three extraction sites: the preAction hook, where the first validation actually runs, the handler wrapper, and the dynamic action. It applies only to extension-created commands, where the listing is the declared flags followed by resolveExtensionCommandInheritedFlagContracts rows (no --no-extensions; read-output controls only with read_output). A core command an extension augments keeps listing its own flags. The dynamic-path zero-flag refusal gets the same code and host-flag list. The error-code catalog and contracts snapshot gain the new unknown_option source.\n\nVerification: the built-CLI spec checks the listing order and exclusions on a non-read command and a read_output command, and the unit specs cover the listing, the typed context and the dynamic path.\n"
